"""Long-session stability (Janas road J-085).

The roadmap text: "Long-session stability. Speculative
generation over the J-033 soak shape: no drift, no state
leakage across rollbacks, memory held."

THE LONG FIXTURE STREAM (the J-033 soak shape, restated
as accounts). J-033's soak is 8 windows of mixed prompts,
256 generated tokens targeted per window, 2,048 total --
a single session cannot reach 2,000 tokens inside a
512-token context, so the soak is repeated session
invocations, session boundaries included. This harness
takes exactly that shape at the account level: 8 segments
(the J-033 windows in order: prose, code, structured,
numbers, instructions, technical, prose2, code2), each a
fresh session invocation starting from its own stated
checkpoint (committed KV length = context count = the
segment's stated prompt length, proposer KV empty, one
stated RNG word for the whole stream), each driven
through J-072's draft loop until its stated plain
continuation is covered exactly. The plain continuation
is 2,224 tokens in total (>= the soak's 2,000 floor,
LONG_MIN_EMITTED), generated by this module's stated
deterministic rule (plain_token), and each round's drafts
are built from it under the segment's acceptance regime:
the would-be prefix lengths cycle through J-079 section
4's filed fixture cycles, themselves shaped from J-075's
filed fixture rows -- HOT [8,6,9,7,8,6,9,5] (English-prose
/ code-like), COLD [1,0,2,1,1,0,1,2] (the Italian-prose
collapse shape), MIXED [3,1,4,0,2,5,1,3] (structured-like
spread). Every number this harness produces is therefore
SIMULATED at fixture level: a property of the stated
stream and the bound machinery, never of any model. The
window-to-row mapping is stated in segment_spec(): the
numbers window files under J-075's structured row and
the instructions window is the stream's Italian-prose
fixture (both answered-locally, doc section 7); every
other window files under its J-033 name's own row.

THE VERDICT RULE (pre-registered here, before the code;
the module's tests grade exactly this):

- (a) NO DRIFT: the concatenated speculative emission
  over the whole stream equals the plain sequential
  account token-for-token -- J-071's
  identity_first_divergence over (speculative, plain)
  is exactly -1 and the lengths are equal. Any other
  divergence index fails the slice, at any position.
- (b) NO STATE LEAKAGE ACROSS ROLLBACKS: after EVERY
  round, the committed state is recomputed from the
  round's pre-draft checkpoint and its J-071 account
  alone, and must match the loop state exactly: KV
  length = checkpoint + accepted + 1; context count =
  checkpoint + accepted + 1; proposer KV (the
  cross-model proposer carries its own, J-071) =
  checkpoint + accepted; the RNG state word is
  UNCHANGED (a greedy round consumes zero draws,
  J-071/J-072); the account's own before/after and
  rollback fields agree with both. The tentative point
  (checkpoint + k + 1) less the account's rollback rows
  must land on the same committed length -- rows past
  it are dead by J-071's read bound, and this harness
  counts any disagreement as leakage. Checks are counted
  per round and again at every segment boundary (final
  KV / context = checkpoint + the segment's full plain
  length, proposer KV = its accepted total, the next
  segment starting from its own stated checkpoint,
  untouched by the last segment's end). Violations are
  counted, never raised past: ZERO is the only passing
  number.
- (c) MEMORY HELD: every bounded structure stays inside
  its pre-registered bound over the whole stream, with
  the bound and the observed maximum reported per
  structure (the suite files both):
  * loop KV length <= LONG_KV_CAPACITY (512, the
    J-033/J-022 context) and context count likewise;
  * one round's verify width <= 16 (the J-035
    draft-check band, read through J-071) and its
    emitted list <= 16 -- per-round accounts are
    transient, folded into scalar totals and the
    emitted product, never retained per round;
  * the J-075 acceptance ledger holds at most
    LONG_LEDGER_ROW_BOUND = 5 rows for this stream's
    one (kind, pair) -- prose x {english, italian,
    other} + code + structured, J-075's full row space
    for one pair -- each row a fixed 3 scalars +
    ACCEPT_HIST_BINS histogram bins (the bin count
    imported from J-075, never restated);
  * the J-079 adaptive controller's and the J-084 loss
    guard's open-window counters stay < their window
    (4 rounds, J-079's quantum) at every post-round
    sample, and their k / totals are scalars;
  * growth accounting closes: the ONLY structure that
    grows over the stream is the ledger's row set
    (bounded above) and the emitted product itself
    (whose length must equal the emitted total exactly
    -- it is the output, not overhead). Overhead units
    are defined as ledger rows x LEDGER_ROW_UNITS;
    the growth over the whole stream must equal
    final_rows x LEDGER_ROW_UNITS exactly (every unit
    of growth is a row creation, nothing else grows),
    and the row count at the last two segment ends must
    be equal and at the bound (the plateau: growth has
    stopped before the stream ends, not merely slowed).
  A bound breach, an unaccounted growth unit, or a
  missing plateau fails the slice. The expert cache's
  resident bound (resident <= budget, J-018/J-024) is
  NOT exercised by this account harness -- no cache sits
  in the J-072 loop's accounts -- and is owned by the
  deferred live leg (doc section 6), where J-033's own
  ceiling rule (a) grades it per window.

BINDINGS (bind, do not duplicate or restate): rounds are
derived by J-071's plan_verify through J-072's
run_loop_round over a real LoopState (the loop's own
rollback assertions stand inside it; this harness's
checkpoint recomputation is the independent outside
check); k is planned by J-079's controller through
J-072's plan_round_k (capacity shortening stays J-072's
recorded plan fact); every speculative round files
through J-075's ledger under the segment's row; every
round feeds J-079's controller and one J-084 loss guard
per segment (per session -- a disabled row's re-enable
is a host act at the next session, J-084's posture,
which the segment boundary performs); the guard's round
price is J-084's step form stated once here (one verify
pass at the plain price LONG_PLAIN_COST plus k draft
steps at LONG_DRAFT_STEP_COST, the worst-case admissible
ratio of J-084 section 1). The sampled form binds by
band: J-082's SAMPLED_K_MAX must equal J-071's band top
(sampling_band_agrees), and this harness's RNG checkpoint
is J-071's greedy zero-draw invariant -- a sampled
long session consumes J-082's stated draws per round
instead and is part of the deferred live leg, not of
this greedy account drive.

WHEN THE GUARD DISABLES MID-SEGMENT: the driver stops
speculating that segment's row and emits the segment's
remaining plain tokens sequentially -- KV and context
advance by one per token, proposer KV and the RNG word
untouched, nothing filed to the ledger, the controller,
or the frozen guard -- and the drift and leakage checks
cover those tokens exactly as they cover speculative
ones. A segment tail shorter than one round (a single
remaining token) takes the same plain path.

WHAT THIS MODULE IS NOT: it executes no forward, times
nothing, opens no device, and contains no speed. No
proposer implementation, verify-pass executor, or
session wiring exists in this tree (G-PROPOSER +
G-EXECUTOR stand, J-083/J-084): require_draft_check_use()
still fails closed and the facade's speculative_generate
still raises not-implemented, so tonight no live long
session can run -- this harness is proven over the
stated fixture stream (SIMULATED), and the live
long-session leg is deferred with its recipe to the
J-086 gate (doc section 6).

HOST CONTRACT (binding on the first live host): (1) one
LoopState per session invocation from its stated
checkpoint, one adaptive controller and one loss guard
per (session, row), one ledger per long session;
(2) per round, snapshot the committed state, plan k
through the controller, run ONE draft-check pass, derive
the round through J-072, then recompute the committed
state from the checkpoint and the account and compare --
a mismatch is leakage: stop, file both states, never
continue over it; (3) on a guard disable, run the row
plain for the rest of the session and file the guard's
disable record beside the run's evidence; (4) at every
session boundary, start from the new session's own
checkpoint and verify the boundary accounts before the
next round; (5) file every round's account, the ledger
rows, the controllers' and guards' counters, and the
bound table (bound + observed maximum per structure)
with the run's evidence.
"""

from core.draft_loss_guard import (
    GUARD_DISABLED,
    LossGuard,
    loss_guard_disabled,
    loss_guard_start,
    record_loss_round,
)
from core.speculative_acceptance import (
    ACCEPT_HIST_BINS,
    LANG_ENGLISH,
    LANG_ITALIAN,
    LANG_NOT_APPLICABLE,
    LANG_OTHER,
    TEXT_CODE,
    TEXT_PROSE,
    TEXT_STRUCTURED,
    AcceptanceLedger,
    record_round,
)
from core.speculative_adaptive import (
    AdaptiveDepth,
    adaptive_initial,
    plan_adaptive_round,
    record_adaptive_round,
)
from core.speculative_loop import (
    LOOP_K_INITIAL,
    KPlan,
    LoopState,
    plan_round_k,
    run_loop_round,
)
from core.speculative_sampling import SAMPLED_K_MAX
from core.speculative_verify import (
    DRAFT_CHECK_MAX_WIDTH,
    PROPOSER_CROSS_MODEL,
    SLOT_CROSS_MODEL,
    VerifyAccount,
    identity_first_divergence,
)

# The J-033 soak shape (header): 8 windows, >= 2,000
# generated tokens across them, prompts <= 200 ids, and
# the J-022 line's 512-token context as the KV capacity.
comptime LONG_SEGMENT_COUNT = 8
comptime LONG_MIN_EMITTED = 2000
comptime LONG_KV_CAPACITY = 512
comptime LONG_PROMPT_MAX = 200

# Acceptance regimes (the segment's fixture cycle source).
comptime REGIME_HOT = 0
comptime REGIME_COLD = 1
comptime REGIME_MIXED = 2

# Drive modes for drive_segment: the controller tunes k,
# or the host states one fixed k for the whole segment
# (a J-083-configured fixed-depth session; the mode the
# hostile-segment test uses to reach the guard's floor).
comptime DRIVE_ADAPTIVE = 0
comptime DRIVE_FIXED = 1

# The loss guard's stated currency for this harness
# (J-084's step form, header): a plain token at 100, a
# k-round at 100 + k * 50 (the worst-case admissible
# drafter of J-084 section 1).
comptime LONG_PLAIN_COST = 100
comptime LONG_DRAFT_STEP_COST = 50

# The ledger bound for this stream's one (kind, pair):
# prose x {english, italian, other} + code + structured
# (J-075's full row space for one pair). One row's size
# in scalar units: rounds + drafted + accepted plus the
# histogram, whose bin count is J-075's own constant.
comptime LONG_LEDGER_ROW_BOUND = 5
comptime LEDGER_ROW_UNITS = 3 + ACCEPT_HIST_BINS

# The draft-mismatch offset: a draft token built as the
# target token + this offset never equals its target.
comptime DRAFT_MISS_OFFSET = 20000


def regime_name(code: Int) raises -> String:
    if code == REGIME_HOT:
        return String("hot")
    if code == REGIME_COLD:
        return String("cold")
    if code == REGIME_MIXED:
        return String("mixed")
    raise Error("LongSessionStability: unknown regime code")


def sampling_band_agrees() -> Bool:
    """J-082's sampled band is J-071's greedy band: the
    correction layer's k cap equals the draft-check band
    top less the pass's one extra position."""
    return SAMPLED_K_MAX == DRAFT_CHECK_MAX_WIDTH - 1


struct SegmentSpec(Copyable, ImplicitlyCopyable):
    """One segment of the long fixture stream: its J-075
    row key, its acceptance regime, its plain length, and
    its prompt length (the session checkpoint)."""

    var text_type: Int
    var language: Int
    var regime: Int
    var plain_len: Int
    var prompt_len: Int

    def __init__(
        out self,
        text_type: Int,
        language: Int,
        regime: Int,
        plain_len: Int,
        prompt_len: Int,
    ):
        self.text_type = text_type
        self.language = language
        self.regime = regime
        self.plain_len = plain_len
        self.prompt_len = prompt_len


def segment_spec(index: Int) raises -> SegmentSpec:
    """The stream's 8 segments, in J-033 window order.

    Plain lengths sum to 2,224 (>= LONG_MIN_EMITTED);
    every prompt is <= LONG_PROMPT_MAX and prompt + plain
    <= LONG_KV_CAPACITY, so every segment fits its
    session's context with margin. The mapping to J-075
    rows is the header's: numbers files as structured,
    instructions is the Italian-prose fixture, technical
    and prose2 file as prose (english / other)."""
    if index == 0:
        return SegmentSpec(TEXT_PROSE, LANG_ENGLISH, REGIME_HOT, 288, 67)
    if index == 1:
        return SegmentSpec(TEXT_CODE, LANG_NOT_APPLICABLE, REGIME_HOT, 288, 54)
    if index == 2:
        return SegmentSpec(
            TEXT_STRUCTURED, LANG_NOT_APPLICABLE, REGIME_MIXED, 288, 48
        )
    if index == 3:
        return SegmentSpec(
            TEXT_STRUCTURED, LANG_NOT_APPLICABLE, REGIME_MIXED, 272, 40
        )
    if index == 4:
        return SegmentSpec(TEXT_PROSE, LANG_ITALIAN, REGIME_COLD, 272, 61)
    if index == 5:
        return SegmentSpec(TEXT_PROSE, LANG_ENGLISH, REGIME_MIXED, 272, 73)
    if index == 6:
        return SegmentSpec(TEXT_PROSE, LANG_OTHER, REGIME_MIXED, 272, 58)
    if index == 7:
        return SegmentSpec(TEXT_CODE, LANG_NOT_APPLICABLE, REGIME_MIXED, 272, 52)
    raise Error("LongSessionStability: segment index outside the stream")


def total_plain_length() raises -> Int:
    """The stream's full plain length, from the specs."""
    var total = 0
    for i in range(LONG_SEGMENT_COUNT):
        total += segment_spec(i).plain_len
    return total


def plain_token(segment: Int, position: Int) -> Int:
    """The stream's stated plain token at one position:
    a fixed arithmetic rule (no table, no RNG), so the
    plain account is reproducible by any reader."""
    return 128 + (segment * 613 + position * 29 + (position // 48) * 7) % 24000


def build_plain_segment(segment: Int) raises -> List[Int]:
    """One segment's plain continuation, by plain_token."""
    var spec = segment_spec(segment)
    var out = List[Int]()
    for pos in range(spec.plain_len):
        out.append(plain_token(segment, pos))
    return out^


def regime_prefix_length(regime: Int, round_index: Int) raises -> Int:
    """The would-be prefix length L for one round: the
    regime's filed fixture cycle (header), one step per
    round. A round at depth k accepts min(k, L)."""
    var idx = round_index % 8
    if regime == REGIME_HOT:
        var hot = List[Int]()
        hot.append(8)
        hot.append(6)
        hot.append(9)
        hot.append(7)
        hot.append(8)
        hot.append(6)
        hot.append(9)
        hot.append(5)
        return hot[idx]
    if regime == REGIME_COLD:
        var cold = List[Int]()
        cold.append(1)
        cold.append(0)
        cold.append(2)
        cold.append(1)
        cold.append(1)
        cold.append(0)
        cold.append(1)
        cold.append(2)
        return cold[idx]
    if regime == REGIME_MIXED:
        var mixed = List[Int]()
        mixed.append(3)
        mixed.append(1)
        mixed.append(4)
        mixed.append(0)
        mixed.append(2)
        mixed.append(5)
        mixed.append(1)
        mixed.append(3)
        return mixed[idx]
    raise Error("LongSessionStability: unknown regime code")


def build_round_drafts(target: List[Int], prefix_len: Int) -> List[Int]:
    """One round's draft list over its target list: the
    first min(k, prefix_len) drafts equal the target (the
    accepted prefix), the rest miss by DRAFT_MISS_OFFSET,
    so J-071's plan_verify derives accepted == min(k,
    prefix_len) exactly. target holds k + 1 tokens; the
    draft list holds k."""
    var k = len(target) - 1
    var drafts = List[Int]()
    for i in range(k):
        if i < prefix_len:
            drafts.append(target[i])
        else:
            drafts.append(target[i] + DRAFT_MISS_OFFSET)
    return drafts^


struct SegmentResult(Copyable):
    """One driven segment's full account: scalar totals,
    the leakage check/violation counts, the closing
    state, the bound maxima observed inside the segment,
    and the emitted tokens (from round accounts and the
    plain fallback only)."""

    var rounds: Int
    var drafted: Int
    var accepted: Int
    var emitted_count: Int
    var fallback_tokens: Int
    var rollback_rows: Int
    var leakage_checks: Int
    var leakage_violations: Int
    var shortened_rounds: Int
    var final_kv: Int
    var final_context: Int
    var final_draft_kv: Int
    var max_kv: Int
    var max_context: Int
    var max_width: Int
    var max_window_rounds: Int
    var min_k_seen: Int
    var max_k_seen: Int
    var adaptive_windows: Int
    var adaptive_deepen: Int
    var adaptive_shallow: Int
    var adaptive_hold: Int
    var guard_disabled: Bool
    var guard_disabled_at_round: Int
    var guard_rounds: Int
    var guard_windows: Int
    var emitted: List[Int]

    def __init__(out self):
        self.rounds = 0
        self.drafted = 0
        self.accepted = 0
        self.emitted_count = 0
        self.fallback_tokens = 0
        self.rollback_rows = 0
        self.leakage_checks = 0
        self.leakage_violations = 0
        self.shortened_rounds = 0
        self.final_kv = 0
        self.final_context = 0
        self.final_draft_kv = 0
        self.max_kv = 0
        self.max_context = 0
        self.max_width = 0
        self.max_window_rounds = 0
        self.min_k_seen = 0
        self.max_k_seen = 0
        self.adaptive_windows = 0
        self.adaptive_deepen = 0
        self.adaptive_shallow = 0
        self.adaptive_hold = 0
        self.guard_disabled = False
        self.guard_disabled_at_round = -1
        self.guard_rounds = 0
        self.guard_windows = 0
        self.emitted = List[Int]()

    def __copyinit__(out self, existing: Self):
        self.rounds = existing.rounds
        self.drafted = existing.drafted
        self.accepted = existing.accepted
        self.emitted_count = existing.emitted_count
        self.fallback_tokens = existing.fallback_tokens
        self.rollback_rows = existing.rollback_rows
        self.leakage_checks = existing.leakage_checks
        self.leakage_violations = existing.leakage_violations
        self.shortened_rounds = existing.shortened_rounds
        self.final_kv = existing.final_kv
        self.final_context = existing.final_context
        self.final_draft_kv = existing.final_draft_kv
        self.max_kv = existing.max_kv
        self.max_context = existing.max_context
        self.max_width = existing.max_width
        self.max_window_rounds = existing.max_window_rounds
        self.min_k_seen = existing.min_k_seen
        self.max_k_seen = existing.max_k_seen
        self.adaptive_windows = existing.adaptive_windows
        self.adaptive_deepen = existing.adaptive_deepen
        self.adaptive_shallow = existing.adaptive_shallow
        self.adaptive_hold = existing.adaptive_hold
        self.guard_disabled = existing.guard_disabled
        self.guard_disabled_at_round = existing.guard_disabled_at_round
        self.guard_rounds = existing.guard_rounds
        self.guard_windows = existing.guard_windows
        self.emitted = existing.emitted.copy()

    def copy(self) -> Self:
        var copied = Self()
        copied.rounds = self.rounds
        copied.drafted = self.drafted
        copied.accepted = self.accepted
        copied.emitted_count = self.emitted_count
        copied.fallback_tokens = self.fallback_tokens
        copied.rollback_rows = self.rollback_rows
        copied.leakage_checks = self.leakage_checks
        copied.leakage_violations = self.leakage_violations
        copied.shortened_rounds = self.shortened_rounds
        copied.final_kv = self.final_kv
        copied.final_context = self.final_context
        copied.final_draft_kv = self.final_draft_kv
        copied.max_kv = self.max_kv
        copied.max_context = self.max_context
        copied.max_width = self.max_width
        copied.max_window_rounds = self.max_window_rounds
        copied.min_k_seen = self.min_k_seen
        copied.max_k_seen = self.max_k_seen
        copied.adaptive_windows = self.adaptive_windows
        copied.adaptive_deepen = self.adaptive_deepen
        copied.adaptive_shallow = self.adaptive_shallow
        copied.adaptive_hold = self.adaptive_hold
        copied.guard_disabled = self.guard_disabled
        copied.guard_disabled_at_round = self.guard_disabled_at_round
        copied.guard_rounds = self.guard_rounds
        copied.guard_windows = self.guard_windows
        copied.emitted = self.emitted.copy()
        return copied^


def drive_segment(
    spec: SegmentSpec,
    plain: List[Int],
    mut ledger: AcceptanceLedger,
    mode: Int,
    fixed_k: Int,
    rng_word: UInt64,
) raises -> SegmentResult:
    """Drive one segment (one session invocation) over
    its plain continuation, under the header's rules.

    Refusals (each before any state is touched): a plain
    list whose length is not the spec's; a prompt outside
    [0, LONG_PROMPT_MAX]; prompt + plain beyond the KV
    capacity; an unknown mode; a fixed k outside the
    proposer's bounds in DRIVE_FIXED. A refusal from
    J-072's loop mid-segment propagates (a fixture or
    capacity defect, never filed as leakage). Leakage and
    drift are COUNTED in the result, not raised: the
    verdict reads the counts.
    """
    if len(plain) != spec.plain_len:
        raise Error(
            "LongSessionStability: the plain list must cover the"
            " segment's stated length exactly"
        )
    if spec.prompt_len < 0 or spec.prompt_len > LONG_PROMPT_MAX:
        raise Error("LongSessionStability: prompt length outside the soak bound")
    if spec.prompt_len + spec.plain_len > LONG_KV_CAPACITY:
        raise Error(
            "LongSessionStability: the segment cannot fit its session's"
            " context; shorten the segment, never truncate it"
        )
    if mode != DRIVE_ADAPTIVE and mode != DRIVE_FIXED:
        raise Error("LongSessionStability: unknown drive mode")
    if mode == DRIVE_FIXED:
        _ = plan_round_k(
            PROPOSER_CROSS_MODEL, fixed_k, spec.prompt_len, LONG_KV_CAPACITY
        )

    var result = SegmentResult()
    var state = LoopState(
        LONG_KV_CAPACITY, spec.prompt_len, spec.prompt_len, rng_word, 0
    )
    var controller = adaptive_initial(PROPOSER_CROSS_MODEL)
    var guard = loss_guard_start(
        PROPOSER_CROSS_MODEL,
        1,
        spec.text_type,
        spec.language,
        LONG_PLAIN_COST,
    )
    result.max_kv = state.kv_length
    result.max_context = state.context_count
    result.min_k_seen = DRAFT_CHECK_MAX_WIDTH

    var pos = 0
    var round_index = 0
    var speculating = True
    while pos < len(plain) and speculating:
        var remaining = len(plain) - pos
        if remaining < 2:
            break
        var plan: KPlan
        if mode == DRIVE_ADAPTIVE:
            plan = plan_adaptive_round(controller, state.kv_length, LONG_KV_CAPACITY)
        else:
            plan = plan_round_k(
                PROPOSER_CROSS_MODEL, fixed_k, state.kv_length, LONG_KV_CAPACITY
            )
        var k = plan.planned_k
        if plan.shortened_for_capacity:
            result.shortened_rounds += 1
        if k > remaining - 1:
            k = remaining - 1
            result.shortened_rounds += 1
        if k < result.min_k_seen:
            result.min_k_seen = k
        if k > result.max_k_seen:
            result.max_k_seen = k
        var target = List[Int]()
        for i in range(k + 1):
            target.append(plain[pos + i])
        var prefix = regime_prefix_length(spec.regime, round_index)
        var drafts = build_round_drafts(target, prefix)
        var snap = state.snapshot()
        var account = run_loop_round(
            state, SLOT_CROSS_MODEL, PROPOSER_CROSS_MODEL, drafts, target, 0
        )
        # (b) the leakage checks: the committed state,
        # recomputed from the checkpoint and the account
        # alone, against the loop state after the round.
        var checks = List[Bool]()
        checks.append(account.kv_before == snap.kv_length)
        checks.append(account.context_before == snap.context_count)
        checks.append(
            state.kv_length == snap.kv_length + account.accepted_count + 1
        )
        checks.append(
            state.context_count
            == snap.context_count + account.accepted_count + 1
        )
        checks.append(
            state.draft_kv_length
            == snap.draft_kv_length + account.accepted_count
        )
        checks.append(state.rng_word == snap.rng_word)
        checks.append(state.rng_word == rng_word)
        checks.append(
            account.kv_rows_to_roll_back == account.k - account.accepted_count
        )
        checks.append(account.kv_after == state.kv_length)
        checks.append(account.context_after == state.context_count)
        checks.append(
            snap.kv_length + account.k + 1 - account.kv_rows_to_roll_back
            == state.kv_length
        )
        for c in range(len(checks)):
            result.leakage_checks += 1
            if not checks[c]:
                result.leakage_violations += 1
        # Bounds observed inside the segment.
        if state.kv_length > result.max_kv:
            result.max_kv = state.kv_length
        if state.context_count > result.max_context:
            result.max_context = state.context_count
        if account.verify_width > result.max_width:
            result.max_width = account.verify_width
        # File the round: ledger (J-075), controller
        # (J-079, adaptive mode only -- a fixed session
        # consults no controller), guard (J-084).
        record_round(ledger, 1, spec.text_type, spec.language, account)
        if mode == DRIVE_ADAPTIVE:
            _ = record_adaptive_round(controller, account)
            if controller.window_rounds > result.max_window_rounds:
                result.max_window_rounds = controller.window_rounds
        var round_cost = LONG_PLAIN_COST + account.k * LONG_DRAFT_STEP_COST
        var decision = record_loss_round(guard, account, round_cost)
        if guard.window_rounds > result.max_window_rounds:
            result.max_window_rounds = guard.window_rounds
        for t in range(len(account.emitted_tokens)):
            result.emitted.append(account.emitted_tokens[t])
        result.rounds += 1
        result.drafted += account.k
        result.accepted += account.accepted_count
        result.emitted_count += account.emitted_count()
        result.rollback_rows += account.kv_rows_to_roll_back
        pos += account.emitted_count()
        round_index += 1
        if decision == GUARD_DISABLED:
            speculating = False
            result.guard_disabled = True
            result.guard_disabled_at_round = guard.disabled_at_round
    # The plain fallback: a disabled row's remainder, or
    # a sub-round tail. KV/context advance by one per
    # token; proposer KV and the RNG word untouched.
    var draft_kv_before_fallback = state.draft_kv_length
    while pos < len(plain):
        result.emitted.append(plain[pos])
        state.kv_length += 1
        state.context_count += 1
        result.fallback_tokens += 1
        result.emitted_count += 1
        pos += 1
    if result.fallback_tokens > 0:
        result.leakage_checks += 1
        if state.draft_kv_length != draft_kv_before_fallback:
            result.leakage_violations += 1
        result.leakage_checks += 1
        if state.rng_word != rng_word:
            result.leakage_violations += 1
        if state.kv_length > result.max_kv:
            result.max_kv = state.kv_length
        if state.context_count > result.max_context:
            result.max_context = state.context_count
    # The segment-boundary accounts (verdict rule (b)):
    # the closing state against the segment's checkpoint
    # plus its full plain length and accepted total.
    result.leakage_checks += 1
    if state.kv_length != spec.prompt_len + spec.plain_len:
        result.leakage_violations += 1
    result.leakage_checks += 1
    if state.context_count != spec.prompt_len + spec.plain_len:
        result.leakage_violations += 1
    result.leakage_checks += 1
    if state.draft_kv_length != result.accepted:
        result.leakage_violations += 1
    result.leakage_checks += 1
    if state.rng_word != rng_word:
        result.leakage_violations += 1
    result.final_kv = state.kv_length
    result.final_context = state.context_count
    result.final_draft_kv = state.draft_kv_length
    if result.rounds == 0:
        result.min_k_seen = 0
    result.adaptive_windows = controller.windows_completed
    result.adaptive_deepen = controller.deepen_events
    result.adaptive_shallow = controller.shallow_events
    result.adaptive_hold = controller.hold_events
    result.guard_rounds = guard.total_rounds
    result.guard_windows = guard.windows_completed
    if loss_guard_disabled(guard) and not result.guard_disabled:
        result.guard_disabled = True
        result.guard_disabled_at_round = guard.disabled_at_round
    return result^


struct StabilityReport(Copyable):
    """The whole long fixture stream's account: the
    verdict rule's three legs as counts and maxima, the
    per-segment ledger growth, and the two token streams
    the drift check compares."""

    var segments: Int
    var rounds: Int
    var drafted: Int
    var accepted: Int
    var emitted: Int
    var fallback_tokens: Int
    var rollback_rows: Int
    var leakage_checks: Int
    var leakage_violations: Int
    var divergence: Int
    var max_kv: Int
    var max_context: Int
    var max_width: Int
    var max_window_rounds: Int
    var min_k_seen: Int
    var max_k_seen: Int
    var shortened_rounds: Int
    var adaptive_windows: Int
    var guard_disables: Int
    var ledger_rows_final: Int
    var ledger_rounds_total: Int
    var overhead_final: Int
    var segment_end_rows: List[Int]
    var segment_end_overhead: List[Int]
    var spec_emitted: List[Int]
    var plain_full: List[Int]

    def __init__(out self):
        self.segments = 0
        self.rounds = 0
        self.drafted = 0
        self.accepted = 0
        self.emitted = 0
        self.fallback_tokens = 0
        self.rollback_rows = 0
        self.leakage_checks = 0
        self.leakage_violations = 0
        self.divergence = -2
        self.max_kv = 0
        self.max_context = 0
        self.max_width = 0
        self.max_window_rounds = 0
        self.min_k_seen = 0
        self.max_k_seen = 0
        self.shortened_rounds = 0
        self.adaptive_windows = 0
        self.guard_disables = 0
        self.ledger_rows_final = 0
        self.ledger_rounds_total = 0
        self.overhead_final = 0
        self.segment_end_rows = List[Int]()
        self.segment_end_overhead = List[Int]()
        self.spec_emitted = List[Int]()
        self.plain_full = List[Int]()

    def __copyinit__(out self, existing: Self):
        self.segments = existing.segments
        self.rounds = existing.rounds
        self.drafted = existing.drafted
        self.accepted = existing.accepted
        self.emitted = existing.emitted
        self.fallback_tokens = existing.fallback_tokens
        self.rollback_rows = existing.rollback_rows
        self.leakage_checks = existing.leakage_checks
        self.leakage_violations = existing.leakage_violations
        self.divergence = existing.divergence
        self.max_kv = existing.max_kv
        self.max_context = existing.max_context
        self.max_width = existing.max_width
        self.max_window_rounds = existing.max_window_rounds
        self.min_k_seen = existing.min_k_seen
        self.max_k_seen = existing.max_k_seen
        self.shortened_rounds = existing.shortened_rounds
        self.adaptive_windows = existing.adaptive_windows
        self.guard_disables = existing.guard_disables
        self.ledger_rows_final = existing.ledger_rows_final
        self.ledger_rounds_total = existing.ledger_rounds_total
        self.overhead_final = existing.overhead_final
        self.segment_end_rows = existing.segment_end_rows.copy()
        self.segment_end_overhead = existing.segment_end_overhead.copy()
        self.spec_emitted = existing.spec_emitted.copy()
        self.plain_full = existing.plain_full.copy()

    def copy(self) -> Self:
        var copied = Self()
        copied.segments = self.segments
        copied.rounds = self.rounds
        copied.drafted = self.drafted
        copied.accepted = self.accepted
        copied.emitted = self.emitted
        copied.fallback_tokens = self.fallback_tokens
        copied.rollback_rows = self.rollback_rows
        copied.leakage_checks = self.leakage_checks
        copied.leakage_violations = self.leakage_violations
        copied.divergence = self.divergence
        copied.max_kv = self.max_kv
        copied.max_context = self.max_context
        copied.max_width = self.max_width
        copied.max_window_rounds = self.max_window_rounds
        copied.min_k_seen = self.min_k_seen
        copied.max_k_seen = self.max_k_seen
        copied.shortened_rounds = self.shortened_rounds
        copied.adaptive_windows = self.adaptive_windows
        copied.guard_disables = self.guard_disables
        copied.ledger_rows_final = self.ledger_rows_final
        copied.ledger_rounds_total = self.ledger_rounds_total
        copied.overhead_final = self.overhead_final
        copied.segment_end_rows = self.segment_end_rows.copy()
        copied.segment_end_overhead = self.segment_end_overhead.copy()
        copied.spec_emitted = self.spec_emitted.copy()
        copied.plain_full = self.plain_full.copy()
        return copied^


def run_long_session(rng_word: UInt64) raises -> StabilityReport:
    """Drive the whole stream: 8 segments in order, one
    shared J-075 ledger, a fresh controller and guard per
    segment (per session), every segment in DRIVE_ADAPTIVE
    from J-072's initial k. The report's divergence is
    J-071's checker over the concatenated streams."""
    var report = StabilityReport()
    var ledger = AcceptanceLedger()
    report.min_k_seen = DRAFT_CHECK_MAX_WIDTH
    for i in range(LONG_SEGMENT_COUNT):
        var spec = segment_spec(i)
        var plain = build_plain_segment(i)
        var res = drive_segment(
            spec, plain, ledger, DRIVE_ADAPTIVE, LOOP_K_INITIAL, rng_word
        )
        report.segments += 1
        report.rounds += res.rounds
        report.drafted += res.drafted
        report.accepted += res.accepted
        report.emitted += res.emitted_count
        report.fallback_tokens += res.fallback_tokens
        report.rollback_rows += res.rollback_rows
        report.leakage_checks += res.leakage_checks
        report.leakage_violations += res.leakage_violations
        report.shortened_rounds += res.shortened_rounds
        report.adaptive_windows += res.adaptive_windows
        if res.guard_disabled:
            report.guard_disables += 1
        if res.max_kv > report.max_kv:
            report.max_kv = res.max_kv
        if res.max_context > report.max_context:
            report.max_context = res.max_context
        if res.max_width > report.max_width:
            report.max_width = res.max_width
        if res.max_window_rounds > report.max_window_rounds:
            report.max_window_rounds = res.max_window_rounds
        if res.rounds > 0 and res.min_k_seen < report.min_k_seen:
            report.min_k_seen = res.min_k_seen
        if res.max_k_seen > report.max_k_seen:
            report.max_k_seen = res.max_k_seen
        for t in range(len(res.emitted)):
            report.spec_emitted.append(res.emitted[t])
        for t in range(len(plain)):
            report.plain_full.append(plain[t])
        var rows_now = len(ledger.rows)
        report.segment_end_rows.append(rows_now)
        report.segment_end_overhead.append(rows_now * LEDGER_ROW_UNITS)
    report.divergence = identity_first_divergence(
        report.spec_emitted, report.plain_full
    )
    report.ledger_rows_final = len(ledger.rows)
    var ledger_rounds = 0
    for i in range(len(ledger.rows)):
        var row = ledger.rows[i].copy()
        ledger_rounds += row.rounds
    report.ledger_rounds_total = ledger_rounds
    report.overhead_final = report.ledger_rows_final * LEDGER_ROW_UNITS
    return report^


def stability_passed(report: StabilityReport) raises -> Bool:
    """The pre-registered verdict rule (header), whole:
    (a) drift -1 with equal lengths at soak scale;
    (b) zero leakage violations; (c) every bound held --
    KV/context inside capacity, width inside the band,
    window counters under the window, ledger rows at or
    under the bound with the closing plateau, growth
    fully accounted by row creation, rollback identity
    exact, and the ledger's rounds equal the driven
    speculative rounds."""
    if report.segments != LONG_SEGMENT_COUNT:
        return False
    if report.emitted < LONG_MIN_EMITTED:
        return False
    if report.emitted != total_plain_length():
        return False
    if len(report.spec_emitted) != report.emitted:
        return False
    if report.divergence != -1:
        return False
    if report.leakage_violations != 0:
        return False
    if report.max_kv > LONG_KV_CAPACITY:
        return False
    if report.max_context > LONG_KV_CAPACITY:
        return False
    if report.max_width > DRAFT_CHECK_MAX_WIDTH:
        return False
    if report.max_window_rounds >= 4:
        return False
    if report.ledger_rows_final > LONG_LEDGER_ROW_BOUND:
        return False
    if report.ledger_rows_final != LONG_LEDGER_ROW_BOUND:
        return False
    var n = len(report.segment_end_rows)
    if n != LONG_SEGMENT_COUNT:
        return False
    if report.segment_end_rows[n - 1] != report.segment_end_rows[n - 2]:
        return False
    if report.segment_end_rows[n - 1] != LONG_LEDGER_ROW_BOUND:
        return False
    if report.overhead_final != report.ledger_rows_final * LEDGER_ROW_UNITS:
        return False
    if report.segment_end_overhead[n - 1] != report.overhead_final:
        return False
    if report.rollback_rows != report.drafted - report.accepted:
        return False
    if report.ledger_rounds_total != report.rounds:
        return False
    return True
